# Drafted by Gemini (R20), edited. R20 Narrator lines: the walking dovecote, the four roosts, and the fights' retries. Triggers: enter:<location or area id>, examine:<prop id>, defeat:<fight id>.
# The Vagrant: second person, present tense, one or two sentences, no game words. Every key has a plain variant.

~ enter:rk_dovecote_r1
| You step inside the walking dovecote, and the floorboards sway gently beneath your boots. Straw, spilled seed, and grey feathers litter the space between stacked crates while a soft cooing hums from above.
| It is a strange thing to stand on the ground floor of a building that is also a bird. The air is thick with the smell of grain and droppings, and stolen letters lie heaped in paper drifts.
once

~ enter:rk_dovecote_r2
| You haul yourself up into the roost floor, where wooden cubbies climb all the way to the low thatch overhead. Every slot is crammed with stolen mail, and a raised platform waits at the far end of the room.
| The air up here is warm and close, smelling of dry down and old parchment. From the shadow of every cubby, a pair of round orange eyes watches you without blinking.
once

~ enter:r2_rafters
| You climb onto the high platform of woven straw and faded cloth, where four open windows let in the night chill. Far below, the dark moor slides past like a slow, silent river.

~ enter:rk_roost_prairie
| The rolling prairie stretches out under the night sky, a sea of gold-grey grass bending in the wind. Out in the middle of the emptiness stands the dark, crooked shape of the dovecote.
| Tall grass whispers round your knees as you walk, dry and restless in the breeze. Above you, a vast night sky keeps its own counsel.
once

~ enter:rk_roost_swamp
| Green-black water pools between dead trees and rattling reeds in the heart of the murky swamp. Out in the shallows, the dovecote stands perched upon its scaly bird legs.
| Pale fog sits low on the still water, smelling of rot and wet moss. Beneath the mist, the dovecote's reflection stands upside down in the dark mirror of the marsh.
once

~ enter:rk_roost_foothills
| Loose scree shifts underfoot in the barren foothills below the Howlers, where the air is thin and cold. Up on a rocky rise, the dovecote perches like a monstrous nest on a cliffside.
| There is naught here but bare rock and a bitter wind that cuts through your cloak. Even so, a faint, steady cooing carries a long way across the stone.
once

~ enter:rk_roost_lakeshore
| Rain hisses down on the shingle along the stormy north shore of Moonsong Lake. Backed by a dark treeline, the dovecote squats upon the wet stones.
| Grey water slaps hard against the beach, throwing up a cold spray. Above you, the rain runs off the dovecote's ragged thatch in thick ropes.
once

~ examine:rk_r1_cord
| Coils of greased leather cord hang here, worked into a hag's stubborn knotwork that has been tied and re-tied over the years.

~ examine:rk_r1_window
| Through the round window, you watch the dark moor sliding steadily past. It is a patient landscape, little minding that it is being walked over.

~ examine:rk_r2_window_a
| The tall window frames a square of open night and rushing wind. When you look down, the ground is a very long way below.

~ defeat:rk_golub
| The hag's high, delighted laughter is the last thing you hear before the dark takes you. A moment later, the roost goes around again.

~ defeat:rk_posse
| A heavy boot, the crack of a cudgel, and the cobbled lane tilts up to meet your face. You wake some time later to the scrape of a key turning in a lock, and not in your favour.

~ defeat:rk_mob_fight
| The ring of torches closes in, and the villagers' chanting fills your ears until there is room for nothing else. The world goes dark at the edges, and the night takes the rest.
